          "distinct": true,
          "id": "07c5081138c372437b06637f7edfab39ef5dd277",
          "message": "fix(site): resolve cross-page /capabilities#theme anchors in the static-export link-check (sq-bpoey) [OPUS-4.8] (#1017)\n\nThe pages.yml \"Link-check the static-export HTML (lychee --offline)\" step has been\nRED on main since #1003: 15 cross-page anchor links to /capabilities#<theme>\n(homepage theme grid + the removed /surface/* redirect stubs) all reported\n\"Cannot find fragment\".\n\nRoot cause (verified empirically against the CI lychee 0.23.0): with --root-dir,\nlychee resolves a *directory* link that carries a fragment to the bare directory\npath (file://<out>/capabilities) and does NOT fall through to that directory's\nindex.html when locating the #fragment heading. ALL of /dir#frag, /dir/#frag and\n/dir/ fail; only an explicit /dir/index.html#frag resolves. So #1003 shipped the\nfirst cross-page fragment links on the site and the self-test only ever covered\nsame-page #anchors.\n\nFix:\n* scripts/check-site-links.sh: add a fragment-aware remap (RULE 0, applied first)\n  that rewrites file://<out>/sparq/<path>#<frag> -> <path>/index.html#<frag>, so\n  lychee locates the fragment in the route's emitted index.html. This is the\n  general fix for every current and future cross-page anchor link. 0 errors over\n  the full export on both lychee 0.23.0 (CI) and 0.24.2.\n* scripts/tests/test_check_site_links.sh: cover the regression both directions —\n  a VALID cross-page fragment now lives in the clean export (Case 1 would have\n  caught #1003), and a new teeth case asserts a dangling cross-page fragment fails.\n* site: capabilityAnchor() + the 8 per-folder redirect stubs now emit the\n  canonical trailingSlash:true form /capabilities/#<theme> and route the stubs\n  through capabilityAnchor() for a single source of truth. (Note: the trailing\n  slash alone does NOT satisfy lychee — RULE 0 is what fixes the gate — but it is\n  the consistent link shape for a trailingSlash:true export and browsers resolve\n  the redirect identically.)\n\nThe <section id=\"...\"> ids in capabilities/page.tsx are unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-21T14:37:05+01:00",
          "tree_id": "797f85a9a47230cb27fdf2e0d1e8e9508ed4cddf",
