          "message": "feat(sparq-kb): PKG natural-language tool envelope + Haiku agent flavor (sq-ve5dy) [OPUS-4.8] (#1085)\n\nReframe PKG access (sq-2m6zm.3) as a natural-language tool call: a cheap-model\n(Haiku) sub-agent does the whole NL -> introspect -> ground -> SPARQL -> run ->\nNL-answer round-trip so the expensive orchestrator only emits the question and\nreads the answer.\n\nThe sound core (`crates/sparq-kb/src/query/nl_tool.rs`, behind the default-OFF\n`query` feature): `run_canned` / `run_raw` -> `NlToolResult` always returning the\nexecuted SPARQL + resolved IRIs + grounding confidence so the caller can verify\nthe answer was computed by the engine, not guessed. Confidence is a structural\nquery-grounding signal (canned / grounded / ungrounded via the live dictionary),\nexplicitly NOT an answer-correctness claim. Ungrounded terms are surfaced with\nedit-distance-ranked same-namespace repair hints.\n\nThe agent flavor (no API key): `.claude/agents/sparq-pkg-nl.md` (`model: haiku`)\ndrives `pkg-query --json`, which emits the envelope. The PRODUCT flavor (sparq\ncalling a configurable cheap-model endpoint) needs sparq's own Anthropic key (an\nexternal-credential dependency) and is deferred.\n\nGates (both feature states): cargo build/clippy --all-targets -D warnings/test\ngreen default (feature OFF) AND --features query/close; rustdoc --all-features\n-D warnings clean; tests exercise the REAL ingested PKG; typos / privacy-claims /\nno-perf-numbers / readme-template clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-21T18:29:47Z",
          "tree_id": "ab33f644083549f71cae411bf552f064574e953a",
